the walking dead's 10th season finale  puts the spotlight on one of the show's  most notorious villains  negan and is full of surprises here's  how the episode plays out  and what it means the episode begins as  negan is exiled from the community he  helped save  he's given a cozy little house outside  of town and asked to not return  while dealing with this unexpected exile  negan has a vision of himself in the  past as a negan we meet at the end of  season six  the presence of this previous version of  himself implies that  while he's clearly changed a bit since  he was defeated and locked away  parts of his old self are still there  past negan chides present-day negan for  trying to win over the alexandrians by  playing nice  it's time to face the facts old man  you are nothing without her  the her here refers to lucille negan's  trusty baseball bat  but of course it also refers to lucille  negan's wife  and the namesake of the bat negan  appears disturbed by the vision but the  next day  he goes to the tree where he believes  his bat was buried after his showdown  with wreck in season 8.  this is when we get our first flashback  to 12 years in the past  negan is tied to a chair and the gang  leader called baxter is interrogating  him about  where he found his supply of chemo drugs  which is somewhat of a rarity in the  post-apocalypse  it's clear that this negan isn't the one  we've come to know later on  he's less self-assured has a hard time  killing walkers  and doesn't quite have that swagger that  has come to define his character  negan begins to tell the story of how he  got the chemo drugs  the drugs negan is carrying came from a  mobile medical clinic  in a flashback he makes a feeble attempt  to rob the clinic's ductus but someone  with a baseball bat quickly knocks him  out  eagle-eyed viewers will recognize his  attacker as laura who later becomes one  of his most trusted allies and the  saviors  when negan comes too he tells franklin  the head of the operation  the story of why he needs the drugs  which begins flashback number three  six weeks further into the past in the  early days of the outbreak  negan is living with his wife lucille  who's undergoing chemotherapy  negan is an attentive and loving husband  however they're quickly running out of  supplies and even though lucille only  has a few rounds of chemo left their  remaining stash of drugs  spoils drawing a fridge malfunction  forcing him to rob the medical clinic  when negan finishes telling his story  they're remarkably generous and kind to  him  they feed him and give him the drugs he  needs telling him they only want to help  people  negan seems genuinely moved by their  generosity thanks to these cascading  flashbacks  fans can finally see aspects of negan's  personality  that were buried in the years that  followed he's more vulnerable without  allies real weapons  or survival skills and it changes how he  interacts with the world  as negan is leading the clinic laura  gives him the familiar baseball bat  they'd previously used to knock him out  but there are even more flashbacks in  the midst of the scenes detailing  lucille's chemo troubles  were taken back to the earliest days of  the outbreak it also introduces a  different moment to negan's personal  growth pre-collapse negan as it turns  out  is a bit of a lout he loses his job as a  gym teacher after beating someone up  and he's spending his days playing video  games he's also cheating on lucille with  one of her friends  something that prevents him from being  with her when she first receives her  cancer diagnosis  it's pretty clear how much lucille's  cancer changed negan  or rather how much his love for lucille  changed him later negan weeps while  lucio recounts how she learned about his  affair  but she tells him that she forgives him  i want you to know that you made up for  it  the episode demonstrates just how  transformative those emotions  were for him during the earliest days of  the apocalypse so how did he then go on  to become the negan we know back in the  first flashback  negan is desperate to bring the chemo  drugs he's carrying back to lucille so  he gives up the location of the mobile  clinic  after the gang rounds up the doctors  they let negan go  lucille had previously begged negan to  forget trying to save her life  and instead just stay with her until she  died when he finally arrives back at  home with the drugs  negan discovers that he should have  listened to her lucille now a walker is  on the bed in their room  she appears to have purposefully  overdosed on pills and tied one arm to  the headboard to prevent her from later  attacking negan  written on the door is a harrowing  phrase please don't leave me like this  it's a crushing moment for negan who's  spent the entire apocalypse trying to  keep lucille alive  after sitting with her for a while he  goes outside to a nearby fence  and uses some barbed wire to put the  final touches on lucille the bat  once he said goodbye to lucille the  person he burns down the house  back at the gang hideout franklin is  being tortured for information  about where he gets his medical supplies  from negan puts us up to it by killing  most of the gang members but leaving  baxter alive  it's here where viewers get their first  glimpse of the negan they know  dressed in his signature leather jacket  and brandishing his bad lucille  negan tells baxter about the man he beat  up who got him fired  but now the rules have changed now  when i see red it's just the question of  what i  am capable of back in the present day  negan digs up lucille the bats and  brings it home to his cabin  he speaks to it as though as lucille  herself apologizing for leaving her  and even apologizing for naming his  baseball bats after her  negan then places lucille the bat into  his fireplace  and watches it burn but things aren't  quite that cut and dry  the next day negan strolls back into  alexandria when carol confronts him he  tells her that he's not interested in  living in exile  carol says that maggie will kill him if  he moves back and makes it clear that  now that she's tried to help negan  she won't intervene negan agrees and  continues on  looking at an infuriated maggie as he  walks by the mischievous grim he wears  while he observes her suggests that  negan's new chapter won't necessarily  include peacemaking based on how season  10 ends it feels inevitable that the  conflict between maggie and negan will  boil over very soon  and that it won't be pretty while  negan's pass reveals that he's a complex  character  and that his propensity for violence is  just one facet of his personality  it also demonstrates that violence is  something that has always existed within  him  even if it's hidden under the surface  check out one of our newest videos right  here  plus even more looper videos about the  walking dead are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

